# gitignore file for gnomon
# ----------------------------------

## Temporary files
*.tmp
*.temp

## Credentials
.git-credentials

## macOS
.DS_Store

## Python Cache
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

## Python Distribution / Packaging
*.egg-info/
*.egg
dist/
build/

## Test Coverage
.coverage
htmlcov/

## Tool Caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/

## Jupyter Notebook
.ipynb_checkpoints/

## Documentation Build
docs/_build/

## Obsidian vault state (json files)
## Machine-local interface state, rewritten on every pane move.
.obsidian/types.json
.obsidian/workspace.json

## Obsidian plugin code. A plugin distribution (`main.js`, `styles.css`, vendored dependencies)
## is downloaded from the community registry and is treated as build output. Two files per
## plugin carry vault configuration and are tracked instead: `manifest.json` fixes the identity
## and version, `data.json` holds the settings. Which plugins are enabled is recorded in
## `.obsidian/community-plugins.json`.
## Consequence: a fresh clone carries the configuration but not the code, so each plugin must
## be reinstalled from the registry. The settings survive, because `data.json` is already in
## place when the plugin loads.
.obsidian/plugins/*/*
!.obsidian/plugins/*/manifest.json
!.obsidian/plugins/*/data.json
